    },
    {
      "source_reference": "Psalms 34:22",
      "target": null,
      "reason": "The request that the God who has seen not remain silent or depart is read within the hostile-witness lament. A broad comparison to divine awareness or rescue alone does not establish a sufficiently distinctive retained link in this pass.",
